;; Primary config: the glossary declares who can act, and the :enforcement
;; levels validate every scenario at planning time, before a browser opens.
;;
;; The :enforcement levels below are the recommended baseline (same as examples
;; 04-06): unknown subjects and interfaces are hard errors; unknown verbs
;; warn (builtin verbs cover the common web actions).
;;
;; Chrome's native password popups (breach warnings, save prompts) are
;; suppressed by the :etaoin adapter's default automation-hygiene prefs —
;; override via :adapter-opts {:prefs {...}} (docs/INSTALL-TIERS.md
;; § adapter-opts).

;; No :glossaries key — the subjects glossary is discovered at the
;; conventional path next to this config (glossary/subjects.edn, i.e.
;; sl/glossary/subjects.edn). An explicit :glossaries map would override
;; the convention wholesale; :glossaries nil turns glossaries off (see
;; shiftlefter-shifted-no-glossary.edn).

{:interfaces {:web {:type :web
                    :adapter :etaoin}}
 :enforcement {:unknown-subject :error
       :unknown-verb :warn
       :unknown-interface :error}}
